WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.990
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:33.700
Tanabata Decorations.

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:37.910
Huh?

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:44.120
There's some delicious looking 
bamboo grass just lying there.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.310
A little taste...

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.710
It's delicious! Oh?

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.260
Jeez...

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:02.190
How wasteful.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.770
Delicious!

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.060
Oh!

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.430
Oh, hi, Panda.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:20.870
What are you going to do 
with this bamboo grass?

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:22.490
Throw a bamboo grass party?

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:25.240
A bamboo grass party?

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:27.830
It's a party with bamboo 
grass everywhere!

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.930
We're going to use it for Tanabata decorations.

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:33.180
Tomorrow's Tanabata.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:35.050
Tanabata?

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:37.830
That would be a windfall <i>(tanabota)</i>.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:40.570
That would be idle gossip <i>(idobata)</i>.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.220
That would be a field 
of flowers <i>(hanabatake)</i>.

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:47.600
Tanabata is a summer festival.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:50.730
It's held once every year.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:53.360
A festival?

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:55.270
So it is a bamboo grass party?

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:56.750
No, it's not.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.430
It's not?

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:06.990
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:10.910
...And then the god was angry, so he

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:13.410
pulled her and Hikoboshi apart, right?

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:20.170
So, Tanabata is for 
Orihime and Hikoboshi...

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:22.620
Onihime, the ogre princess?

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.650
Why is there a scary person?

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:30.140
So when Hikoboshi, Orihime 
and Onihime are united,

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:33.580
they form the Summer Triangle in the night sky.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.890
That's not it.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:37.180
So it's a love triangle?

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:38.280
That's not it, either!

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:43.450
So when Hikoboshi and Orihime...

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.750
It's so good!

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:48.840
Hey now, are you listening?

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:52.380
I'm listening to the story of 
the oni's love triangle.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.740
That's not it. Jeez.

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:58.760
You're the one who asked me 
to explain Tanabata to you.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:02.110
So when do you eat the bamboo grass?

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.640
I'm trying to tell you 
that you don't eat it.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.770
You hang lots of
 paper decorations on it,

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:12.010
and then you hang strips of paper
 with wishes written on them.

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:16.590
But if you put all that stuff on there,

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:18.610
it'll be in the way when you're eating.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:20.670
You're not listening at all.

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.200
I'm saying that you don't 
eat that bamboo grass.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.210
You need to tell me that first.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:28.580
I have been!

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:32.290
If you hang up your wish and 
don't eat the bamboo grass,

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.750
your wish will come true.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:36.710
Any wish?

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:38.700
If it's a small one.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:42.760
What? No big wishes?

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.370
Maybe a medium-sized one.

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:47.340
What are you talking about?

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.520
Hey, Miss Sasako.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:55.400
Is that the paper you write your wish on?

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:59.150
Oh, I'm making decorations.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:02.990
Wow, that looks fun.

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:04.840
Do you want to try too, Panda?

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:07.730
Yes, I do!

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:13.530
Hello.

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:16.370
Here you go.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.790
Oh, thank you.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:26.340
Are you off from the 
zoo today, Mr. Handa?

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:27.920
Huh? Y-Yes.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:30.300
You've been coming by a lot recently.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:33.780
Uh, no... I mean, uh, yes.

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:37.190
W-When I come here...

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:42.750
Yes?

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:47.100
Uh, um...

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:50.010
It calms my heart or something...

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:51.740
Oh, I see.

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.730
Oh! Then I should probably 
leave you alone.

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:57.550
Please take your time.

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:10.230
Hey, Miss Sasako,
 how do you do this?

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:11.480
What's the matter?

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:13.900
I can't even tell how you made that.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.520
In a way, he's really talented.

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:20.120
Oh, don't say things like that.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:24.470
Listen carefully. First, you fold 
it from this end, like this...

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:25.840
Like this?

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:27.460
The other way, Panda.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:29.410
And then you fold that three times...

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:33.410
I'm finished!

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:36.360
What is that?

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:38.590
It's a panda!

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:40.380
Oh, I see.

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:42.840
Well, at least it's black and white.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:45.130
Here you go, Miss Sasako.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:48.190
We'll leave the decorations for later,

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:50.050
and work on the strips of paper next.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.050
The ones you write your wish on?

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:54.510
Yup.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:56.970
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:06.170
Go ahead and write your wish on here.

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:08.670
If you bring it back by tomorrow night,

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:10.300
I'll hang it on the bamboo grass.

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:15.020
So I write up to a 
medium-sized wish on here?

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:17.760
I think you can write whatever you want.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:21.030
Oh, really? Anything?

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:22.920
Anything.

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:27.570
I wonder what I should wish for!

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.680
Here's one for you, too, Mr. Penguin.

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:38.010
You're so serious.

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:38.990
Yeah.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.570
You can write whatever you want, right?

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:45.110
I can't write whatever about 
my feelings toward Miss Penko!

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.570
I don't think one strip 
is going to be enough.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.560
Could you give me ten, Miss Sasako?

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:54.240
Huh?

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:56.370
That's not fair.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:59.240
Then could I get twenty?

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:01.710
It's just one per person.

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:09.180
Here you go.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:16.650
W-What is it?

00:08:17.170 --> 00:08:19.050
Here's one for you, Mr. Handa.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.600
A strip of paper to write 
your wish on, for Tanabata.

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:32.500
Thank you very much.

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:36.060
We'll be open late tomorrow 
because of Tanabata.

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:38.580
Oh, okay.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:40.300
See you then.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.800
I wonder what I should wish for.

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:57.800
Maybe I should wish that I can eat
 a lot of bamboo grass.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:01.160
You already always eat 
a lot of it, Panda.

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:03.870
What did you write, Mr. Penguin?

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:05.670
I haven't written anything yet.

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:08.260
You only get one, so it's hard, you know?

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:13.230
I wonder what everyone else is writing?

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:20.110
I want a wife...

00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:24.120
No, before that, 
I need a girlfriend.

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:27.120
Pardon me.

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:31.050
Yes, one moment please!

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:39.330
Miss Sasako is so cute.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:54.920
I-I'm sorry. Um, it's nothing...

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:58.080
Did you hear what I just said, Panda?

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:01.700
I agree, totally cute.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:05.390
Er, that's not the only reason 
why I come here, though!

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:07.880
The coffee is really good, too.

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:11.610
You can see me all you want 
at the zoo, Mr. Handa.

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:15.010
Yet you come here just 
to see cute, little me.

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:19.210
Jeez.

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:24.990
I am totally cute.

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:28.520
No, I'm saying that Miss Sasako is cute.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:36.560
Miss Sasako.

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:39.450
Guess what.

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:44.050
Don't!

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:46.340
Why?

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:48.570
I don't know her that well yet!

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:50.440
Really?

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:51.880
Yes!

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:54.370
Okay.

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:01.340
Hey, Miss Sasako,

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:07.770
what do you think of guys
who like to take care of animals?

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:13.710
And how about a guy built sort of like a panda?

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:12.560
P-Panda!

00:11:13.710 --> 00:11:14.820
Come here! Over here!

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:18.030
What are they doing?

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:23.090
Who knows.

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:36.920
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:41.930
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:40.900
Panda's Wish.

00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:46.680
Oh, Mr. Handa said that?

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:47.930
Yeah.

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:51.540
I wonder why he doesn't just say it.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:54.350
Well, Mr. Handa is a late bloomer.

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:55.880
Really?

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:59.730
He's full of knowledge 
from magazines and such,

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:03.820
but when it comes to the 
real thing, he chickens out.

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:06.930
I totally know what you're talking about.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:09.870
What was it, "living vicariously"?

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:13.530
Would you stop making mistakes 
that are hard to retort?

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:18.840
I want to give Mr. Handa 
some advice. Any ideas?

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:21.890
What? You're asking me?

00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:26.070
Well, you're full of experience, 
Mr. Full-time Panda.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:27.670
Since you're twice divorced.

00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:31.140
I've asked you not to go around saying
 I've been divorced twice.

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:36.610
But you know, we have a discerning 
eye regarding couples.

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:41.030
Well, that's true.

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:45.940
A lot of the visitors who come here 
happen to be couples.

00:12:45.940 --> 00:12:47.850
Yeah.

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:51.000
The couples out on their 
first date are so innocent.

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:55.560
Sometimes they can't even hold hands.

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:56.960
I know.

00:12:57.830 --> 00:13:02.240
Then there are those 
couples that are fighting.

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:05.470
They make it so obvious.

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:06.630
Really?

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:09.610
Like those two heading over here.

00:13:09.610 --> 00:13:12.450
There's some uneasiness 
surrounding them right now.

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:16.900
Wow, you're right.

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:20.180
But just watch.

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:23.000
Once they see us...

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:26.500
Look, pandas!

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:27.740
Let's go!

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:33.560
Wow! They're so cute!

00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:34.790
Right?

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:35.560
Yeah.

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:41.890
So where should we go next?

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:42.710
See? All better.

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:46.370
You're amazing, Mr. Full-time Panda.

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:48.410
You think so?

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:51.790
Nothing less from a Latino.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:55.230
You're giving me weird 
characteristics again.

00:13:56.030 --> 00:14:01.600
Please give me advice, 
Mr. Full-time Manual Labor Panda!

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:05.080
You're making it hard to retort again.

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:09.840
Well, I guess one piece of advice is...

00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:12.620
it's important to take that step forward.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:17.950
Dosukoi!

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:24.490
I don't see love brewing there.

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:27.020
Why are they sumo wrestling?

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:28.730
They're not going to?

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:29.890
Of course not!

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:34.900
The important thing about love 
is assertiveness <i>(sekkyokusei)</i>.

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:40.150
Oh, so they have to be 
preachy <i>(sekkyo kusei)</i>?

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:42.720
Really?

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:46.650
You just imagined something 
really weird again, didn't you?

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:48.580
I said, "assertiveness."

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:44.040
Thanks for all your hard work!

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:46.050
Thanks!

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:48.300
Thank you.

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:52.630
So,

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:55.900
Mr. Full-time Panda, who is full 
of experience regarding love,

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:58.270
gave me some advice for you.

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:00.100
Huh? He did?

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:03.190
Are you interested?

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:06.690
H-Huh? Not really...

00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:10.650
Well, nevermind, then.

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:11.150
Huh?

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:15.570
W-Well, I'll hear it just in case...

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:18.540
Today's

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:18.540
Tanabata

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:18.540
Day!

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:24.350
What's wrong?

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:30.380
May I 
get a 
girlfriend.

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:33.620
<i>But I'd be really embarrassed</i>

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:36.700
<i>if I hung this up and Miss Sasako saw it.</i>

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:40.350
What are you worrying about?

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:44.000
Come on! What's important 
in love is assertiveness!

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:45.400
Take that step forward!

00:16:46.210 --> 00:16:47.900
P-Panda!

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:51.820
Hello!

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:54.140
Welcome!

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:56.370
Oh, Panda and Mr. Handa.

00:16:56.760 --> 00:16:59.330
Yoohoo!

00:16:56.970 --> 00:16:59.330
T-Thanks for having us.

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:02.740
Perfect timing.

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:04.010
For what?

00:17:04.010 --> 00:17:06.210
We were just getting done 
putting up the decorations.

00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:09.170
This is the last one.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:12.330
It's the decoration I made!

00:17:13.020 --> 00:17:15.620
Well then, let's put it at the very top.

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:21.630
Next, we'll be putting 
up all of the wishes!

00:17:22.550 --> 00:17:25.170
Everyone, please come up!

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:28.330
What did you write?

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:29.060
Want to see?

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:32.480
Stop 
global 
warming.

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:32.190
Stop global warming.

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:34.180
Wow.

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:36.110
It's a very serious matter.

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:37.700
This is mine!

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:41.660
May 
Miss Penko 
confess her 
love to me.

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:41.660
May Miss Penko confess her love to me.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:43.730
That's rather shameless.

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:46.570
Oh, what should I do if she asks me out?!

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:47.900
I don't know what to do!

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:49.260
I don't know what to do!

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:50.510
I don't know what to do!

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:51.630
Which is it?

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:59.600
World peace

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:02.560
No eating 
too much.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:05.520
Get 
rid 
of my 
fussiness.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:08.480
I want 
to ride 
a bike.

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:11.440
First place 
in a 
marathon.

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:28.830
May many 
customers 
come to 
Polar Bear's 
Café.

00:18:33.450 --> 00:18:36.350
Did you write your wish, Mr. Handa?

00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:40.390
Well, um...

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:44.830
Um, that's...

00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:49.320
What's important in 
love is assertiveness!

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:08.910
I did write one.

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:11.580
Then please hang it up.

00:19:13.310 --> 00:19:14.080
Okay.

00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:20.300
May I 
get a 
girlfriend.

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:26.360
You don't have a girlfriend, Mr. Handa?

00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:30.230
I don't.

00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:32.410
I see.

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:36.120
I hope you find one soon!

00:19:47.010 --> 00:19:47.980
Thanks.

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:53.470
Last call!

00:19:57.700 --> 00:20:00.370
Did you put your wish up, Panda?

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:03.310
Oh!

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:05.380
Jeez, did you forget?

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:09.330
What should I write?

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:13.990
Let's see...

00:20:13.990 --> 00:20:17.190
May my legs get long.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:19.370
